          "filename": "Hereford mappa mundi 14th cent repro IMG 3895.JPG",
          "caption": "The Hereford map is a mappa mundi, or world map, from the 1300s. It is found above the altar in Hereford cathedral, England. The letters M-O-R-S (\"death\") are encircling the map, reminding the viewer of his mortality. The map contains lots of mythological information of the depicted places, seen from a Christian perspective. Replica..",
